    <statement><p>Simplify the complex fraction
<me>{
\frac{\displaystyle \; \frac{1}{x}+\frac{5}{x^2}\;}{\displaystyle \frac{10}{y}+\frac{11}{y^2}}
}</me>
in the form <m>\frac{A}{B}</m>.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>A =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> and <m>B =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y^{2}\mathopen{}\left(1x+5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x^{2}\mathopen{}\left(10y+11\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
